window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b151-134181ec349c4188.json"]={sha256:"134181ec349c4188202dc63f40e222064293329558c5f5fa3500f45517ca8059",value:{"id":"b151","title":"隧道噴射混凝土支護","titleEn":"Shotcrete tunnel support","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以早齡承載、基面黏結與厚度控制噴凝土支護為主線，從薄殼受力與岩面接觸與早齡強度與卸載時序建立系統邊界，再把鋼筋網背後的陰影區、芯樣方向與強度換算連到分區品質與交接證據。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 十單元以可核算的模型和可追溯證據逐步判讀不同失效。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on control shotcrete support through early strength, substrate bond and installed thickness. It begins with Shell action and rock contact and Early strength and unloading sequence, links Shadows behind reinforcement mesh and Core orientation and strength interpretation, and ends with Zoned quality and handover evidence. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. Ten units use reproducible models and traceable evidence to distinguish failure mechanisms.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-support","subcategoryTitle":"岩體支護與襯砌","subcategoryTitleEn":"Rock support and tunnel linings","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-support","learningTags":["underground","ug-support","support"],"architectureFamily":"support","architectureNodes":[["薄殼受力與岩面接觸","Shell action and rock contact"],["回彈量與材料收支","Rebound and material balance"],["鋼筋網背後的陰影區","Shadows behind reinforcement mesh"],["芯樣方向與強度換算","Core orientation and strength interpretation"],["分區品質與交接證據","Zoned quality and handover evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"support","labels":["薄殼受力與岩面接觸","回彈量與材料收支","鋼筋網背後的陰影區","芯樣方向與強度換算","分區品質與交接證據"],"labelsEn":["Shell action and rock contact","Rebound and material balance","Shadows behind reinforcement mesh","Core orientation and strength interpretation","Zoned quality and handover evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例所有輸入均為教學假設。首先檢查薄殼受力與岩面接觸：N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa；再獨立檢查早齡強度與卸載時序：utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75。壓力由 0.10 增為 0.11 MPa，半徑和厚度不變，環力由 0.40 增為 0.44 MN/m，應力由 2.67 增為 2.93 MPa；這只適用完整環。 兩個結果不能自動組成完整設計，因為噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 將把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時作為模型以外的驗證證據，並保留原始紀錄與尚待確認的邊界。","textEn":"All inputs in this integrated example are teaching assumptions. First check Shell action and rock contact: N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa. Independently check Early strength and unloading sequence: utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75. Increasing pressure from 0.10 to 0.11 MPa at fixed radius and thickness raises ring force from 0.40 to 0.44 MN/m and stress from 2.67 to 2.93 MPa, for an intact ring only. The two results are not a complete design because the layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. Use synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps as evidence independent of the calculation, retaining raw records and unverified boundaries.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b151-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」與「早齡強度與卸載時序」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shell action and rock contact\" and \"Early strength and unloading sequence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b151-v14-01","title":"薄殼受力與岩面接觸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shell action and rock contact: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shell action and rock contact” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"黏結完整的噴層限制岩塊轉動，把局部作用傳給周圍岩體及岩栓。若岩面存在空腔，膜力路徑會局部轉成彎曲，平均壓應力合格仍可能有背面拉裂；完整圓環模型只用來辨認量級，不能代替節理岩塊的穩定分析。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較；若出現未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A bonded layer restrains block rotation and transfers local actions to surrounding rock and bolts. Cavities convert membrane transfer into bending, allowing back-face tension despite acceptable mean compression. An intact-ring model establishes scale only and does not replace joint-block stability analysis. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints. If concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shell action and rock contact” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shell action and rock contact”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-01-k1","title":"薄殼受力與岩面接觸","titleEn":"Shell action and rock contact","text":"黏結完整的噴層限制岩塊轉動，把局部作用傳給周圍岩體及岩栓。若岩面存在空腔，膜力路徑會局部轉成彎曲，平均壓應力合格仍可能有背面拉裂；完整圓環模型只用來辨認量級，不能代替節理岩塊的穩定分析。","textEn":"A bonded layer restrains block rotation and transfers local actions to surrounding rock and bolts. Cavities convert membrane transfer into bending, allowing back-face tension despite acceptable mean compression.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shell action and rock contact\" is correct?","options":["平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸","黏結完整的噴層限制岩塊轉動，把局部作用傳給周圍岩體及岩栓。","材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載"],"optionsEn":["Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact","A bonded layer restrains block rotation and transfers local actions to surrounding rock and bolts.","A set material can already carry the full design load"],"answer":1,"explanation":"黏結完整的噴層限制岩塊轉動，把局部作用傳給周圍岩體及岩栓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A bonded layer restrains block rotation and transfers local actions to surrounding rock and bolts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b151-v14-02","title":"薄殼受力與岩面接觸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shell action and rock contact: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shell action and rock contact” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shell action and rock contact\", which statement holds?","options":["拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同","平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處","原創教學假設：N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes","Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored","Original teaching assumptions: N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: N=pR=0.10 MPa*4 m=0.40 MN/m; sigma=N/t=0.40/0.15=2.67 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b151-v14-03","title":"薄殼受力與岩面接觸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shell action and rock contact: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shell action and rock contact” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shell action and rock contact\"?","options":["將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力"],"optionsEn":["Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b151-v14-04","title":"薄殼受力與岩面接觸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shell action and rock contact: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shell action and rock contact” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較；若出現未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將雷射斷面、敲擊空鼓圖與岩塊節理位置對齊比較，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare laser sections and sounding maps registered to rock-block joints to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄殼受力與岩面接觸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shell action and rock contact\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落。","材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness.","A set material can already carry the full design load"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未接觸區的集中彎曲造成裂紋，表面厚度正常仍可能剝落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concentrated bending over noncontact zones cracks a layer of apparently normal thickness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b151-v14-05","title":"早齡強度與卸載時序：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Early strength and unloading sequence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「早齡強度與卸載時序」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Early strength and unloading sequence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"凝結只是材料開始形成骨架，不代表已達長期承載。開挖卸載與噴層硬化同時發生，下一循環擾動可能作用在仍弱的拱頂；室溫試件與潮濕寒冷岩面的成熟度不同，須用齡期和溫度描述同一強度狀態。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對；若出現溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「早齡強度與卸載時序」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Setting starts formation of a material skeleton rather than providing long-term capacity. Excavation unloading competes with hardening, and the next disturbance can reach a weak crown. Laboratory and cold wet rock-face maturity differ, so age and temperature must describe a common strength state. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time. If warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Early strength and unloading sequence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75.","failure":"常見誤解：「材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A set material can already carry the full design load\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「早齡強度與卸載時序」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Early strength and unloading sequence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-05-k1","title":"早齡強度與卸載時序","titleEn":"Early strength and unloading sequence","text":"凝結只是材料開始形成骨架，不代表已達長期承載。開挖卸載與噴層硬化同時發生，下一循環擾動可能作用在仍弱的拱頂；室溫試件與潮濕寒冷岩面的成熟度不同，須用齡期和溫度描述同一強度狀態。","textEn":"Setting starts formation of a material skeleton rather than providing long-term capacity. Excavation unloading competes with hardening, and the next disturbance can reach a weak crown.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A set material can already carry the full design load Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「早齡強度與卸載時序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Early strength and unloading sequence\" is correct?","options":["材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載","泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量","凝結只是材料開始形成骨架，不代表已達長期承載。"],"optionsEn":["A set material can already carry the full design load","Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock","Setting starts formation of a material skeleton rather than providing long-term capacity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"凝結只是材料開始形成骨架，不代表已達長期承載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Setting starts formation of a material skeleton rather than providing long-term capacity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b151-v14-06","title":"早齡強度與卸載時序：定量估算","titleEn":"Early strength and unloading sequence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「早齡強度與卸載時序」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Early strength and unloading sequence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「早齡強度與卸載時序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Early strength and unloading sequence\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75。","表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆","不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75.","A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh","Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: utilization=stress/strength=0.60/1.20=0.50; at strength=0.80 MPa it becomes 0.75. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b151-v14-07","title":"早齡強度與卸載時序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Early strength and unloading sequence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「早齡強度與卸載時序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Early strength and unloading sequence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「早齡強度與卸載時序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Early strength and unloading sequence\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對。","沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time.","A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b151-v14-08","title":"早齡強度與卸載時序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Early strength and unloading sequence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「早齡強度與卸載時序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Early strength and unloading sequence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對；若出現溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A set material can already carry the full design load\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將早齡貫入或拔釘結果與原位溫度及噴射時間配對，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to match early penetration or stud results to in-place temperature and spraying time to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「早齡強度與卸載時序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Early strength and unloading sequence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量","溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock","Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫暖試件高估拱頂強度，使後續擾動造成不可逆微裂縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Warm specimens overstate crown strength and subsequent disturbance creates irreversible microcracks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b151-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「回彈量與材料收支」與「基面黏結與破壞界面」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rebound and material balance\" and \"Bond and failure interfaces\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b151-v14-09","title":"回彈量與材料收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rebound and material balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「回彈量與材料收支」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rebound and material balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"回彈物不是原配比的等比例縮小，骨材與纖維可能選擇性流失。泵送量只能描述供料，不能證明留在岩面的密度或纖維含量；材料帳應區分落地回彈、管路殘留與有效噴層，才可把厚度不足與輸送損失分開。 判別這個機制時，應觀察以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積；若出現回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回彈量與材料收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rebound is not a scaled copy of the original mix because aggregate and fibres can be preferentially lost. Pumped volume does not prove installed density or fibre content. Separate rebound, line residue and retained layer so insufficient thickness can be distinguished from delivery losses. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume. If reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rebound and material balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回彈量與材料收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rebound and material balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-09-k1","title":"回彈量與材料收支","titleEn":"Rebound and material balance","text":"回彈物不是原配比的等比例縮小，骨材與纖維可能選擇性流失。泵送量只能描述供料，不能證明留在岩面的密度或纖維含量；材料帳應區分落地回彈、管路殘留與有效噴層，才可把厚度不足與輸送損失分開。","textEn":"Rebound is not a scaled copy of the original mix because aggregate and fibres can be preferentially lost. Pumped volume does not prove installed density or fibre content.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回彈量與材料收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rebound and material balance\" is correct?","options":["回彈物不是原配比的等比例縮小，骨材與纖維可能選擇性流失。","泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量","拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Rebound is not a scaled copy of the original mix because aggregate and fibres can be preferentially lost.","Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock","Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"回彈物不是原配比的等比例縮小，骨材與纖維可能選擇性流失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rebound is not a scaled copy of the original mix because aggregate and fibres can be preferentially lost. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b151-v14-10","title":"回彈量與材料收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Rebound and material balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回彈量與材料收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rebound and material balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回彈量與材料收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rebound and material balance\", which statement holds?","options":["平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處","原創教學假設：Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3。","量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力"],"optionsEn":["Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored","Original teaching assumptions: Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3.","Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Vretained=Vsupplied*(1-r)=12 m3*(1-0.18)=9.84 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b151-v14-11","title":"回彈量與材料收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rebound and material balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回彈量與材料收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rebound and material balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回彈量與材料收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rebound and material balance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道","以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining","Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b151-v14-12","title":"回彈量與材料收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rebound and material balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回彈量與材料收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rebound and material balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積；若出現回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以分區回彈收集重量及原位密度反算留存體積，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to use zoned rebound mass and in-place density to reconstruct retained volume to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回彈量與材料收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rebound and material balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"回彈重新混入會引入污染並掩蓋纖維與骨材比例改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reintroduced rebound brings contamination and conceals changed fibre and aggregate proportions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b151-v14-13","title":"基面黏結與破壞界面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bond and failure interfaces: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「基面黏結與破壞界面」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bond and failure interfaces” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"粉塵、水膜與鬆動薄片會切斷噴層和基岩之間的剪力傳遞。拉拔量到的是試體中最弱路徑，可能位於膠層、噴凝土或岩石；相同峰值不代表相同修復方法，必須保留破壞面照片和各層位置才能判讀。 判別這個機制時，應觀察逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置；若出現膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基面黏結與破壞界面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dust, water films and loose flakes interrupt shear transfer to the substrate. A pull test samples the weakest path, which may lie in adhesive, shotcrete or rock. Equal peaks need not imply equal repairs; retain failure-face photographs and layer positions for interpretation. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test. If adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bond and failure interfaces” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「基面黏結與破壞界面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bond and failure interfaces”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-13-k1","title":"基面黏結與破壞界面","titleEn":"Bond and failure interfaces","text":"粉塵、水膜與鬆動薄片會切斷噴層和基岩之間的剪力傳遞。拉拔量到的是試體中最弱路徑，可能位於膠層、噴凝土或岩石；相同峰值不代表相同修復方法，必須保留破壞面照片和各層位置才能判讀。","textEn":"Dust, water films and loose flakes interrupt shear transfer to the substrate. A pull test samples the weakest path, which may lie in adhesive, shotcrete or rock.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基面黏結與破壞界面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bond and failure interfaces\" is correct?","options":["拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同","粉塵、水膜與鬆動薄片會切斷噴層和基岩之間的剪力傳遞。","表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆"],"optionsEn":["Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes","Dust, water films and loose flakes interrupt shear transfer to the substrate.","A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh"],"answer":1,"explanation":"粉塵、水膜與鬆動薄片會切斷噴層和基岩之間的剪力傳遞。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dust, water films and loose flakes interrupt shear transfer to the substrate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b151-v14-14","title":"基面黏結與破壞界面：定量估算","titleEn":"Bond and failure interfaces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「基面黏結與破壞界面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bond and failure interfaces” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基面黏結與破壞界面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bond and failure interfaces\", which statement holds?","options":["不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換","沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能","原創教學假設：bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable","A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support","Original teaching assumptions: bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: bondStress=F/A=25 kN/0.025 m2=1.0 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b151-v14-15","title":"基面黏結與破壞界面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bond and failure interfaces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「基面黏結與破壞界面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bond and failure interfaces” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基面黏結與破壞界面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bond and failure interfaces\"?","options":["逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸"],"optionsEn":["Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b151-v14-16","title":"基面黏結與破壞界面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bond and failure interfaces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「基面黏結與破壞界面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bond and failure interfaces” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置；若出現膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐件記錄拉拔破壞面、濕度及切割邊界位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to record the failure plane, moisture and isolation-cut boundary for every pull test to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基面黏結與破壞界面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bond and failure interfaces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換。","表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement.","A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh"],"answer":1,"explanation":"膠層剝離被錯當噴凝土失效，會導致錯誤的材料更換。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adhesive debonding misclassified as shotcrete failure leads to the wrong material replacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b151-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」與「局部厚度與斷面配準」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh\" and \"Local thickness and section registration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b151-v14-17","title":"鋼筋網背後的陰影區：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shadows behind reinforcement mesh” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鋼筋網交叉點遮蔽噴流，外觀平順的表面可能蓋住相連蜂窩。網距、岩面凹凸與噴層厚度一起決定包覆難度；含網試板若沒有重現交叉節點，就只能驗材料，不能驗證現地幾何下的密實程度。 判別這個機制時，應觀察切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙；若出現沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mesh intersections shield the stream, and a smooth face can hide connected voids. Spacing, rock roughness and thickness jointly control encapsulation. A panel without representative intersections tests material but cannot verify consolidation within the installed geometry. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections. If connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shadows behind reinforcement mesh” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shadows behind reinforcement mesh”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-17-k1","title":"鋼筋網背後的陰影區","titleEn":"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh","text":"鋼筋網交叉點遮蔽噴流，外觀平順的表面可能蓋住相連蜂窩。網距、岩面凹凸與噴層厚度一起決定包覆難度；含網試板若沒有重現交叉節點，就只能驗材料，不能驗證現地幾何下的密實程度。","textEn":"Mesh intersections shield the stream, and a smooth face can hide connected voids. Spacing, rock roughness and thickness jointly control encapsulation.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh\" is correct?","options":["表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆","平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處","鋼筋網交叉點遮蔽噴流，外觀平順的表面可能蓋住相連蜂窩。"],"optionsEn":["A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh","Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored","Mesh intersections shield the stream, and a smooth face can hide connected voids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鋼筋網交叉點遮蔽噴流，外觀平順的表面可能蓋住相連蜂窩。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mesh intersections shield the stream, and a smooth face can hide connected voids. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b151-v14-18","title":"鋼筋網背後的陰影區：定量估算","titleEn":"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shadows behind reinforcement mesh” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3。","量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力","只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3.","Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state","One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: voidFraction=0.012 m3/0.30 m3=0.04=4 percent; solidVolume=0.288 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b151-v14-19","title":"鋼筋網背後的陰影區：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shadows behind reinforcement mesh” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙。","材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections.","A set material can already carry the full design load"],"answer":1,"explanation":"切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b151-v14-20","title":"鋼筋網背後的陰影區：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shadows behind reinforcement mesh” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙；若出現沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到切開含相同網距的試板，統計交叉點背面的孔隙，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to section panels with matching mesh spacing and quantify voids behind intersections to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼筋網背後的陰影區」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shadows behind reinforcement mesh\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處","沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored","Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿鋼筋連通的孔洞讓水快速進入並加速局部腐蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Connected voids along reinforcement admit water rapidly and accelerate local corrosion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b151-v14-21","title":"局部厚度與斷面配準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Local thickness and section registration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「局部厚度與斷面配準」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Local thickness and section registration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岩面起伏使同一材料體積產生不同的最薄厚度，局部彎曲與耐久往往由薄區主導。施工前後點雲必須共用控制基準，否則岩面突起會被誤讀為新增厚度；平均料量只能作總體收支，不能取代最薄處驗證。 判別這個機制時，應觀察將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比；若出現點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「局部厚度與斷面配準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rock roughness gives different minimum thicknesses at equal material volume, while local bending and durability often depend on thin areas. Before-and-after clouds require common control; otherwise protrusions appear as added thickness. Delivered volume is a global balance rather than verification of local minima. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum. If cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Local thickness and section registration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「局部厚度與斷面配準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Local thickness and section registration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-21-k1","title":"局部厚度與斷面配準","titleEn":"Local thickness and section registration","text":"岩面起伏使同一材料體積產生不同的最薄厚度，局部彎曲與耐久往往由薄區主導。施工前後點雲必須共用控制基準，否則岩面突起會被誤讀為新增厚度；平均料量只能作總體收支，不能取代最薄處驗證。","textEn":"Rock roughness gives different minimum thicknesses at equal material volume, while local bending and durability often depend on thin areas. Before-and-after clouds require common control; otherwise protrusions appear as added thickness.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「局部厚度與斷面配準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Local thickness and section registration\" is correct?","options":["岩面起伏使同一材料體積產生不同的最薄厚度，局部彎曲與耐久往往由薄區主導。","平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處","不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換"],"optionsEn":["Rock roughness gives different minimum thicknesses at equal material volume, while local bending and durability often depend on thin areas.","Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored","Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"岩面起伏使同一材料體積產生不同的最薄厚度，局部彎曲與耐久往往由薄區主導。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rock roughness gives different minimum thicknesses at equal material volume, while local bending and durability often depend on thin areas. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b151-v14-22","title":"局部厚度與斷面配準：定量估算","titleEn":"Local thickness and section registration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「局部厚度與斷面配準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Local thickness and section registration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「局部厚度與斷面配準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Local thickness and section registration\", which statement holds?","options":["沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能","原創教學假設：tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m。","平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸"],"optionsEn":["A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support","Original teaching assumptions: tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m.","Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: tavg=V/A=15 m3/100 m2=0.15 m; assumed local minimum=0.09 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b151-v14-23","title":"局部厚度與斷面配準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Local thickness and section registration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「局部厚度與斷面配準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Local thickness and section registration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「局部厚度與斷面配準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Local thickness and section registration\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量","將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock","Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b151-v14-24","title":"局部厚度與斷面配準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Local thickness and section registration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「局部厚度與斷面配準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Local thickness and section registration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比；若出現點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到將厚度釘、鑽芯與雙期點雲在共同基準下互比，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare thickness pins, cores and two-epoch clouds on a common datum to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「局部厚度與斷面配準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Local thickness and section registration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換"],"optionsEn":["Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"點雲錯位遮蔽薄區，造成局部剛度與保護層被高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cloud misregistration conceals thin zones and overstates local stiffness and cover. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b151-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「芯樣方向與強度換算」與「收斂與噴層應變零點」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Core orientation and strength interpretation\" and \"Convergence and strain-gauge zero\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b151-v14-25","title":"芯樣方向與強度換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Core orientation and strength interpretation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「芯樣方向與強度換算」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Core orientation and strength interpretation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"噴凝土有層間界面，取芯方向會改變荷載穿越界面的方式。端面不平又會引入偏心壓縮，兩種效應都能降低峰值但原因不同；試體形狀、齡期與飽水狀態必須一起記錄，不能把任意立方體結果直接套到拱頂。 判別這個機制時，應觀察成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態；若出現端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「芯樣方向與強度換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sprayed layers contain interfaces whose loading depends on coring direction. Uneven ends introduce eccentric compression; both effects reduce peaks for different reasons. Record geometry, age and saturation together rather than transferring an arbitrary cube result directly to the crown. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations. If eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Core orientation and strength interpretation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「芯樣方向與強度換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Core orientation and strength interpretation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-25-k1","title":"芯樣方向與強度換算","titleEn":"Core orientation and strength interpretation","text":"噴凝土有層間界面，取芯方向會改變荷載穿越界面的方式。端面不平又會引入偏心壓縮，兩種效應都能降低峰值但原因不同；試體形狀、齡期與飽水狀態必須一起記錄，不能把任意立方體結果直接套到拱頂。","textEn":"Sprayed layers contain interfaces whose loading depends on coring direction. Uneven ends introduce eccentric compression; both effects reduce peaks for different reasons.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「芯樣方向與強度換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Core orientation and strength interpretation\" is correct?","options":["不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換","噴凝土有層間界面，取芯方向會改變荷載穿越界面的方式。","量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力"],"optionsEn":["Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable","Sprayed layers contain interfaces whose loading depends on coring direction.","Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state"],"answer":1,"explanation":"噴凝土有層間界面，取芯方向會改變荷載穿越界面的方式。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sprayed layers contain interfaces whose loading depends on coring direction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b151-v14-26","title":"芯樣方向與強度換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Core orientation and strength interpretation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「芯樣方向與強度換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Core orientation and strength interpretation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「芯樣方向與強度換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Core orientation and strength interpretation\", which statement holds?","options":["只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道","材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載","原創教學假設：fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining","A set material can already carry the full design load","Original teaching assumptions: fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: fc=F/A=200 kN/(pi*0.05^2 m2)=25.46 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b151-v14-27","title":"芯樣方向與強度換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Core orientation and strength interpretation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「芯樣方向與強度換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Core orientation and strength interpretation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「芯樣方向與強度換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Core orientation and strength interpretation\"?","options":["成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b151-v14-28","title":"芯樣方向與強度換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Core orientation and strength interpretation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「芯樣方向與強度換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Core orientation and strength interpretation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態；若出現端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到成組比較相同齡期但不同取芯方向的破壞形態，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to compare failure shapes of same-age cores taken in different orientations to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「芯樣方向與強度換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Core orientation and strength interpretation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題。","量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems.","Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state"],"answer":1,"explanation":"端面偏心造成假低強度，掩蓋真正的層間黏結問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Eccentric end loading produces false low strength and obscures actual interlayer bond problems. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b151-v14-29","title":"收斂與噴層應變零點：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Convergence and strain-gauge zero: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「收斂與噴層應變零點」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Convergence and strain-gauge zero” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地層在噴層安裝前已變形，總收斂並不全部進入噴凝土。應變計晚歸零會刪除早期荷載，溫度又能造成非機械應變；需把噴射、安裝、歸零與後續開挖放在同一時間軸，才可比較環向收縮和材料應力。 判別這個機制時，應觀察把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時；若出現歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「收斂與噴層應變零點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ground deforms before support installation, so total convergence does not all enter the lining. Late zeroing removes early load history, and temperature adds nonmechanical strain. Align spraying, installation, zeroing and excavation before comparing circumferential shortening with material stress. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps. If a calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Convergence and strain-gauge zero” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「收斂與噴層應變零點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Convergence and strain-gauge zero”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-29-k1","title":"收斂與噴層應變零點","titleEn":"Convergence and strain-gauge zero","text":"地層在噴層安裝前已變形，總收斂並不全部進入噴凝土。應變計晚歸零會刪除早期荷載，溫度又能造成非機械應變；需把噴射、安裝、歸零與後續開挖放在同一時間軸，才可比較環向收縮和材料應力。","textEn":"Ground deforms before support installation, so total convergence does not all enter the lining. Late zeroing removes early load history, and temperature adds nonmechanical strain.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「收斂與噴層應變零點」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Convergence and strain-gauge zero\" is correct?","options":["量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力","沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能","地層在噴層安裝前已變形，總收斂並不全部進入噴凝土。"],"optionsEn":["Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state","A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support","Ground deforms before support installation, so total convergence does not all enter the lining."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地層在噴層安裝前已變形，總收斂並不全部進入噴凝土。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ground deforms before support installation, so total convergence does not all enter the lining. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b151-v14-30","title":"收斂與噴層應變零點：定量估算","titleEn":"Convergence and strain-gauge zero: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「收斂與噴層應變零點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Convergence and strain-gauge zero” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「收斂與噴層應變零點」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Convergence and strain-gauge zero\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa。","平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸","泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa.","Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact","Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: epsilon=0.8 mm/4000 mm=0.0002; sigma=10 GPa*0.0002=2 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b151-v14-31","title":"收斂與噴層應變零點：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Convergence and strain-gauge zero: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「收斂與噴層應變零點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Convergence and strain-gauge zero” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If a calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「收斂與噴層應變零點」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Convergence and strain-gauge zero\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時。","表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps.","A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b151-v14-32","title":"收斂與噴層應變零點：失效診斷","titleEn":"Convergence and strain-gauge zero: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「收斂與噴層應變零點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Convergence and strain-gauge zero” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時；若出現歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量測儀器歸零就表示結構回到無應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Zeroing a sensor returns the structure to a stress-free state\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到把應變、溫度、收斂及儀器歸零時刻共同對時，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to synchronize strain, temperature, convergence and gauge-zero timestamps to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「收斂與噴層應變零點」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Convergence and strain-gauge zero\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能","歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support","A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"歸零後曲線平穩卻漏掉累積應力，錯判支護已卸載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A calm post-zero curve hides accumulated stress and falsely suggests unloading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b151-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「活動裂縫與耐久通路」與「分區品質與交接證據」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Active cracks and durability paths\" and \"Zoned quality and handover evidence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b151-v14-33","title":"活動裂縫與耐久通路：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Active cracks and durability paths: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「活動裂縫與耐久通路」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Active cracks and durability paths” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"裂縫寬度描述某一時刻，無法單獨區分乾縮、溫度循環與岩體持續運動。水和侵蝕離子可沿裂縫優先進入，封閉表面可能把出水轉移到別處；維修判斷需追蹤同一裂縫的開合、水量及附近收斂歷史。 判別這個機制時，應觀察以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置；若出現活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「活動裂縫與耐久通路」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Width describes an instant rather than distinguishing shrinkage, thermal cycling and continued rock movement. Water and aggressive ions follow cracks, while sealing a face can redirect discharge. Repair decisions need the same crack's opening, flow and neighbouring convergence history. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs. If an active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Active cracks and durability paths” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day.","failure":"常見誤解：「沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「活動裂縫與耐久通路」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Active cracks and durability paths”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-33-k1","title":"活動裂縫與耐久通路","titleEn":"Active cracks and durability paths","text":"裂縫寬度描述某一時刻，無法單獨區分乾縮、溫度循環與岩體持續運動。水和侵蝕離子可沿裂縫優先進入，封閉表面可能把出水轉移到別處；維修判斷需追蹤同一裂縫的開合、水量及附近收斂歷史。","textEn":"Width describes an instant rather than distinguishing shrinkage, thermal cycling and continued rock movement. Water and aggressive ions follow cracks, while sealing a face can redirect discharge.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「活動裂縫與耐久通路」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Active cracks and durability paths\" is correct?","options":["裂縫寬度描述某一時刻，無法單獨區分乾縮、溫度循環與岩體持續運動。","沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能","只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道"],"optionsEn":["Width describes an instant rather than distinguishing shrinkage, thermal cycling and continued rock movement.","A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support","One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining"],"answer":0,"explanation":"裂縫寬度描述某一時刻，無法單獨區分乾縮、溫度循環與岩體持續運動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Width describes an instant rather than distinguishing shrinkage, thermal cycling and continued rock movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b151-v14-34","title":"活動裂縫與耐久通路：定量估算","titleEn":"Active cracks and durability paths: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「活動裂縫與耐久通路」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Active cracks and durability paths” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「活動裂縫與耐久通路」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Active cracks and durability paths\", which statement holds?","options":["材料已經凝結就能承受全部設計荷載","原創教學假設：openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day。","拉拔數字相同就代表破壞原因完全相同"],"optionsEn":["A set material can already carry the full design load","Original teaching assumptions: openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day.","Equal pull-test values prove identical failure causes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: openingRate=(0.30-0.18) mm/30 day=0.004 mm/day. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b151-v14-35","title":"活動裂縫與耐久通路：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Active cracks and durability paths: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「活動裂縫與耐久通路」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Active cracks and durability paths” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If an active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If an active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「活動裂縫與耐久通路」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Active cracks and durability paths\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","平均厚度合格便能忽略所有局部薄處","以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Passing mean thickness permits every local thin area to be ignored","Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b151-v14-36","title":"活動裂縫與耐久通路：失效診斷","titleEn":"Active cracks and durability paths: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「活動裂縫與耐久通路」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Active cracks and durability paths” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置；若出現活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If an active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沒有漏水的裂縫一定不影響支護性能」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dry crack cannot affect the performance of tunnel support\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到以裂縫計、水量、溫度和固定視角照片追蹤同一位置，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to track one location with crack gauges, flow, temperature and fixed-view photographs to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「活動裂縫與耐久通路」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Active cracks and durability paths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道"],"optionsEn":["An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining"],"answer":0,"explanation":"活動裂縫被當成乾縮封補後重新開裂並改變漏水位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An active crack treated as shrinkage reopens and shifts the leakage location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b151-v14-37","title":"分區品質與交接證據：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Zoned quality and handover evidence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「分區品質與交接證據」如何影響隧道噴射混凝土支護的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Zoned quality and handover evidence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shotcrete tunnel support”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支護品質沿里程與環向都可能不同，將所有試件合併平均會失去對薄區和濕區的辨識。交接資料應連結地質、批次、噴射時刻和缺陷處置，讓後續裂紋能追溯到初期狀態，而不是只留下單一平均強度證明。 判別這個機制時，應觀察逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄；若出現缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分區品質與交接證據」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Quality varies along chainage and around the perimeter; pooling specimens conceals thin or wet zones. Link geology, batches, spraying times and defect disposition so later cracks can be traced to their initial condition rather than a single average-strength certificate. Use the following check to discriminate the mechanism: Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone. If unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Zoned quality and handover evidence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分區品質與交接證據」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Zoned quality and handover evidence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-37-k1","title":"分區品質與交接證據","titleEn":"Zoned quality and handover evidence","text":"支護品質沿里程與環向都可能不同，將所有試件合併平均會失去對薄區和濕區的辨識。交接資料應連結地質、批次、噴射時刻和缺陷處置，讓後續裂紋能追溯到初期狀態，而不是只留下單一平均強度證明。","textEn":"Quality varies along chainage and around the perimeter; pooling specimens conceals thin or wet zones. Link geology, batches, spraying times and defect disposition so later cracks can be traced to their initial condition rather than a single average-strength certificate.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分區品質與交接證據」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Zoned quality and handover evidence\" is correct?","options":["只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道","支護品質沿里程與環向都可能不同，將所有試件合併平均會失去對薄區和濕區的辨識。","平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸"],"optionsEn":["One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining","Quality varies along chainage and around the perimeter; pooling specimens conceals thin or wet zones.","Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"支護品質沿里程與環向都可能不同，將所有試件合併平均會失去對薄區和濕區的辨識。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Quality varies along chainage and around the perimeter; pooling specimens conceals thin or wet zones. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b151-v14-38","title":"分區品質與交接證據：定量估算","titleEn":"Zoned quality and handover evidence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分區品質與交接證據」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Zoned quality and handover evidence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent。噴層與岩塊、岩栓共同工作，空腔會改變受力路徑。 此結果僅用來核對量綱及模型敏感度，不是專案設計值、實測紀錄或現場允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent. The layer interacts with rock blocks and bolts; cavities change its load path. This checks dimensions and model sensitivity; it is neither measured project data nor a design or acceptance value.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分區品質與交接證據」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Zoned quality and handover evidence\", which statement holds?","options":["泵送纖維含量就是岩面留存的纖維含量","表面平順便足以證明鋼筋網完全包覆","原創教學假設：coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent。"],"optionsEn":["Pump-feed fibre content equals fibre content retained on the rock","A smooth face proves complete encapsulation of reinforcement mesh","Original teaching assumptions: coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: coverage=verifiedZones/requiredZones=18/20=0.90=90 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b151-v14-39","title":"分區品質與交接證據：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Zoned quality and handover evidence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分區品質與交接證據」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Zoned quality and handover evidence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply the following check at handover: Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","failure":"注意干擾：缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄。量測須保存位置、時間及基準，讓同條件的重複結果可比較；並特別檢查「缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查」是否能由這組資料區分。儀器校核與誤差估計應先於判讀，由負責技師核定該項試驗的允收和停留點。","textEn":"Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone. Retain position, time and datums for comparable repeats, specifically distinguishing this scenario: Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected. Instrument checks and uncertainty estimates precede interpretation; the responsible engineer sets acceptance and hold points for this test.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄列為該構件的交接證據，連結到施工位置、材料批次及判讀版本。若發現缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查，先保留原始紀錄並由負責技師確認處置，不能以本課算例替代核定作業計畫。","textEn":"Apply the following check at handover: Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone. Link results to location, material batch and interpretation version. If unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected, retain original records and obtain the responsible engineer's disposition; this example does not replace an approved work plan.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分區品質與交接證據」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Zoned quality and handover evidence\"?","options":["逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","不同尺寸與方向的試體強度都可以直接互換"],"optionsEn":["Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Strengths from different specimen sizes and orientations are directly interchangeable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b151-v14-40","title":"分區品質與交接證據：失效診斷","titleEn":"Zoned quality and handover evidence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"prerequisiteIds":["b151-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分區品質與交接證據」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Zoned quality and handover evidence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：判別這個機制時，應觀察逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄；若出現缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查，便須重新檢查原先假設的接觸、力或水的傳遞邊界，而不能只調整計算結果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected, revisit the assumed contact, force or water-transfer boundary rather than merely adjusting the calculated result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要有一份合格報告就能代表整條隧道」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One passing report represents the entire tunnel lining\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b151-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查。相似表徵也可能由量測偏差造成，因此應回到逐區核對厚度、黏結、早齡強度及缺陷關閉紀錄，以獨立證據判別原因；只修補可見症狀將留下原本的傳力或滲流問題。","textEn":"Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected. Similar symptoms can arise from measurement bias: return to audit thickness, bond, early strength and defect closure by zone to discriminate the cause. Treating visible symptoms alone leaves the original transfer or seepage problem unresolved.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]},{"id":"b151-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分區品質與交接證據」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Zoned quality and handover evidence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查。","平均厚度足夠便不必查岩面接觸"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected.","Adequate mean thickness removes the need to check rock contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺少里程對應的合格報告無法證明受損區曾受檢查。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unlocated passing reports cannot establish that a damaged zone was inspected. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-underground","v14s-cedd-g4","v14s-efnarc","v14s-sika-tunnel"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
